ntiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{6{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{|\\sqrt{6}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{6}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06349d8e-8391-574b-b6ee-d09717af159e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247480} {:answer/id #uuid "28b08c9d-77c7-5bea-8de3-24e47c4a6b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247786} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4c8ae4-b8b1-5ed2-b232-73c90f37ed26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248097} {:answer/id #uuid "97ffb8aa-ac92-5db2-a3d4-4a6b34576f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{8}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248778} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b1dd01-2ffe-53eb-9456-1dfad676593b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28b08c9d-77c7-5bea-8de3-24e47c4a6b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247786} :answer-field/id #uuid "f124bfeb-924c-5974-b5d6-5bac9d8b7458" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d978df6a-8484-5ed1-885e-b4758185514d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114056" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{8}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{8}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{8}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{|x|\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8\\sqrt{8}}{|\\sqrt{8}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{8}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "243323f6-ad70-573c-a08a-406469d3a0ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247740} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7538ae-df96-5bd6-89c4-eb9b39dfc0b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247852} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf8e15f-3174-57fb-b8e4-5d360ff846f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248257} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8775a6-08c9-5e68-8ded-0ebea2805076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248846} {:answer/id #uuid "a3358706-6bfa-540b-8aac-27669d842b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bf8e15f-3174-57fb-b8e4-5d360ff846f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248257} :answer-field/id #uuid "6296fb51-a261-5315-98e2-bafc87eb4fd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4d360a8-fe79-5362-9972-fed2a1994303" :question/math-academy-id "q-114074" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $(4x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd84a82-8cbc-585f-8bbe-ce19fdb09a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247954} {:answer/id #uuid "47871075-deb3-513b-8a8e-3639234f622c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248060} {:answer/id #uuid "983ebb92-bd83-5ed1-a0f3-8fe2c8c188ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248782} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c31917-04d7-582e-b1d4-e26865d402a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248917} {:answer/id #uuid "af0b67fe-7271-56c8-8367-495b25ff2f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7c31917-04d7-582e-b1d4-e26865d402a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248917} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f9281c-e5d7-5f72-ac5c-0b25153c48f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8425d47-32c7-547c-ab87-ac1c6071e1e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114078" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/8)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{8}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/\\sqrt{8})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012323fc-4e7b-5948-bd33-ac6535cdacea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247423} {:answer/id #uuid "275108dc-ba21-516f-8c42-bd8bf8d71064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247772} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab5218b-e36e-59ff-8b03-f71a3f5c4374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247944} {:answer/id #uuid "82b6c265-2f3d-5dbe-b622-87847517b9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248580} {:answer/id #uuid "afcf5a5d-6b1c-5e07-b91a-41eca607a863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcf5a5d-6b1c-5e07-b91a-41eca607a863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249002} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f84de4-1a81-5ce2-ac8e-5901c4a2a352" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c216ad6d-32f4-5235-ae6f-6f4e1e6db054" :question/math-academy-id "q-114080" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250187 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b573ef-1007-53ad-a1f4-f1bbb6a97f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247434} {:answer/id #uuid "21345a50-5601-54ac-b6b8-8854f3bcf25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247719} {:answer/id #uuid "21932059-2779-56bb-aff8-46d2133806aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247722} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ca1c00-7abb-53af-b061-a218e5f95af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249025} {:answer/id #uuid "fe379fad-f57a-50e1-ad28-7deffbfbf656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b573ef-1007-53ad-a1f4-f1bbb6a97f3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247434} :answer-field/id #uuid "20529d1c-5c66-5379-87b8-bf5bcb3ca23c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d206bd2a-2b8b-589e-945a-46c1dd7ed6d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-114084" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+(x/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi }{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ace781-d274-5e56-a670-5a4a11cc396e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}^{3}\\text{ arcsin }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247581} {:answer/id #uuid "5692d53f-e590-5c4b-b3cf-b26aac77396a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248210} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc18efd-3204-5471-89ef-885c34415cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsin }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249128} {:answer/id #uuid "d2dad63e-a18d-5765-8de3-fdf0ca004d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}^{3}\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249295} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4b608f-ffe9-5210-b69f-f21778e1a218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-7\\text{ arctan }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5692d53f-e590-5c4b-b3cf-b26aac77396a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248210} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b1cbd54-3439-59c4-a3d8-a241f241223c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb0e1654-81f3-51ff-a1ad-22ecef08f60d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114164" :question/problem "$\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+7(\\text{ arcsec }x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+7\\text{ arcsec }x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263a6676-bcc6-56f2-bf75-5b204a0665c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247761} {:answer/id #uuid "8afc0f1b-1e0c-5d92-a062-0d61fc9caadd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248663} {:answer/id #uuid "9369dced-f14b-556e-945e-9f6e682f7d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248734} {:answer/id #uuid "945bb0e9-9cf8-5d4f-a7ae-aab444d3de81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248744} {:answer/id #uuid "f074aa68-1eb8-5f6d-8644-d4e407e90daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f074aa68-1eb8-5f6d-8644-d4e407e90daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249535} :answer-field/id #uuid "916b2a0c-4759-5859-ac15-e71d9797d8fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca385184-ef23-5e09-850b-a334c3c5908a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114168" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" :question/worked-solution "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(0-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250206 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9fbe19-cf60-531c-baf0-c504de2ac80c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247524} {:answer/id #uuid "19c56598-e8ce-5d22-8ffa-5f30dd11841a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247660} {:answer/id #uuid "57c92f5d-6664-5cf7-9fc7-0643b248d475" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248221} {:answer/id #uuid "5d314c53-79f8-54f8-b84b-eae20722ae51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248272} {:answer/id #uuid "c6cc8340-3010-5529-9554-55c7d0dc7818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19c56598-e8ce-5d22-8ffa-5f30dd11841a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247660} :answer-field/id #uuid "366d90ae-e6be-58b7-a32f-61ddab4f0f9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "646baf8c-2fc5-5cdc-90e1-2b00b50de1be" :question/math-academy-id "q-114202" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{y}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}-3(-{y}^{-1}){|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2(-1-(-2))+3(\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{1}{(-2)}) \\\\  & =2(-1+2)+3(-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2(1)+3(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "459929b5-16a5-5034-94f0-b9e58f15ceec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248048} {:answer/id #uuid "64343e0f-0dc4-59b1-9b42-e034415d89e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248328} {:answer/id #uuid "81c1316f-a38a-5e2e-b549-e63e68e66f54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248573} {:answer/id #uuid "a9fe39d8-722a-5b08-a7b5-69095e8360bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248934} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7cabaa-8d3a-58ef-b215-67b7a26ae5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "459929b5-16a5-5034-94f0-b9e58f15ceec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248048} :answer-field/id #uuid "e640f0ef-8ce1-5b26-8c98-c9b2965485ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d22fa8db-1712-5866-9e2b-91e93589e8f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114245" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}^{′}}{{[{x}^{2}-2x+1]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1-x+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x-2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}^{′}}{{[2x-2]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01827748-212d-560e-98f3-b45c7c8273e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247428} {:answer/id #uuid "124ecb28-d039-500b-a460-c817f5999b13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247589} {:answer/id #uuid "954f57bf-be13-5e8b-bc74-e37ff744e3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248753} {:answer/id #uuid "a2878e25-4fd1-52ce-b0a3-685f50cbf8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248875} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1a3389-4f89-55ad-9187-e9cc38d950e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01827748-212d-560e-98f3-b45c7c8273e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247428} :answer-field/id #uuid "14fa5bf4-26c0-5e7f-8772-8b5826495a67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1490f312-92c6-56e8-8f14-6e1263bd40da" :question/math-academy-id "q-114249" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=-1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1]}^{′}}{{[{x}^{2}+2x+1]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)}{2x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)}{2x+2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)]}^{′}}{{[2x+2]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x+2})}{2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{1}{2(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26da406a-b1ee-533c-8e84-f3f3308fd3a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247767} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} {:answer/id #uuid "b96beb80-9254-5797-a25b-3e85eaa45af7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{3{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249082} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8237c1-5f1b-5b27-84a1-36bf62527629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249105} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f75f10-d4ff-5f2b-8f08-23ed364814bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ddb17e-a21a-5bc8-bdfe-e5654290dd4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a75c4b14-7006-556e-bd1e-e4613f35b446" :question/math-academy-id "q-114287" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a625e0-f342-5d88-863b-2cc610f12c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x-1){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247918} {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} {:answer/id #uuid "4d558edc-f058-5d64-aa0f-acff177c0e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-3x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248117} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa27907-71bc-5690-9d5a-5ea98a3a03cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248503} {:answer/id #uuid "cd15176c-1580-5959-a4f3-0332eefaf817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2-x){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} :answer-field/id #uuid "f37b9f98-70f3-5724-8992-60b01c3a21f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1022e01f-7a5a-562e-a877-5ba5b3c9edd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114293" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x-4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x-4)\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-3){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0251f12b-0bcd-5543-9eb5-f4ec7e4c9752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} {:answer/id #uuid "7229d8df-ae59-5660-b41e-cae11851e04c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248420} {:answer/id #uuid "91224b99-89c4-59ce-b789-19a10d61178d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248714} {:answer/id #uuid "dc01fc34-a583-577b-8fdc-401ef22073b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249369} {:answer/id #uuid "f20a32cf-99d1-5344-b1f0-7a8da3242cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{csc}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0251f12b-0bcd-5543-9eb5-f4ec7e4c9752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247439} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec890aa8-f649-5040-b0db-08c864882cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de415510-24b2-53a0-b8c3-ddc9cdee62b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-114294" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identities $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ and rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{3}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,⟹\\,-\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{u}^{3}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{3}⁡x}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{sec}^{3}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6729e761-a109-51c4-8606-18751a53f95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248350} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf1abf3-9f83-5499-84e8-2cdbf9e21301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248682} {:answer/id #uuid "aeaf0778-2cce-5ff4-8bd6-a8910cbdb116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248985} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e5714-4c05-5edb-b661-6e6122f8d589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7740ab9-c0ff-5f8c-91e3-87881adad76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a77892-fbcb-5fb9-802a-ce425028c881" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3878ae79-1e5e-59bf-8bb6-ae0cf3aaa4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247928} {:answer/id #uuid "5f75b493-3947-527e-a588-60cab80d2be3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248287} {:answer/id #uuid "74e4c221-78c2-5702-af4f-442e99facd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248451} {:answer/id #uuid "cef45258-9cb1-562e-a7e4-faf62bbc7406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249259} {:answer/id #uuid "e0dd153a-e09b-5898-9188-70f04b5e8044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3878ae79-1e5e-59bf-8bb6-ae0cf3aaa4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247928} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b71088-363e-519b-b126-45df5c59e3e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40079a0f-e072-5ffd-a039-30e177ed76fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-114304" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d87cf2-ba4e-5ee2-b888-16334d204447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247661} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfa8fa7-c8a9-5491-a85f-a85434d1131e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247678} {:answer/id #uuid "5b42bf75-0d9b-5855-aac9-9999790d5338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248251} {:answer/id #uuid "a03cb483-a296-5946-8a8d-952eac55cad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248855} {:answer/id #uuid "aedb9126-7c6d-5c55-ad4b-869a319638e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d87cf2-ba4e-5ee2-b888-16334d204447" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\sqrt{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247661} :answer-field/id #uuid "0416b7bd-da37-58c6-8855-48ba00ca405e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edc6fd62-64ca-5ae7-b219-55728bf85a2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114306" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we use the fact that $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
